            <title>[LU-21237] osd-ldiskfs: T10-PI guards ignore segment offset within page</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21237</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;osd_dif_generate() and osd_dif_verify() (lustre/osd-ldiskfs/osd_integrity.c) take the client guards for a bio integrity segment from lnb-&amp;gt;lnb_guards&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;0&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;, whatever the segment's offset in its page (bv_offset). osd_bio_integrity_compare() does the same. tgt_checksum_niobuf_t10pi() sets lnb_guard_rpc for full-page writes whose checksum type matches the device's T10 type, so those guards are used.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When a bio segment starts in the middle of a page, the sectors after that point get the guards of the start of the page. Depending on whether the device checks guards on write, the write then fails with a protection error, or a later read fails verification.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This can only happen with PAGE_SIZE larger than the filesystem block size (64 KiB pages with 4 KiB blocks, aarch64 or ppc64le servers), a T10-PI capable device and the client T10 guards in use. osd_do_bio() starts a bio in the middle of a page after a transaction restart in the middle of a page (dr_start_pg_wblks) or at a gap in the disk blocks inside a page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A fix would offset the guard pointer by offset_in_page(data_buf) / interval for the segment (and the same in verify and compare), or fall back to computing the guard when the segment does not start the page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Found while reviewing &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69823" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69823&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20994" title="osd-ldiskfs: end bios on RAID row boundaries" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20994"&gt;LU-20994&lt;/a&gt;), which could have added a third way to start a bio in the middle of a page (a RAID row cut). That patch now never cuts a row that starts inside a page.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
